{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "useDefineForClassFields": true,
    "module": "ESNext",
    /*
      No DOM: this package speaks about a request body, and the only body type it names is Node's `Buffer`.
      Nothing in it needs a browser's declarations, and pulling them in would also demand `DOM.Iterable` for
      `FetcherHeaders`' iterator members.
    */
    "lib": ["ES2022"],
    "types": ["node"],
    /*
      Read third-party declarations instead of waving at them — the opposite of the other four packages here,
      and deliberate: this package ships nothing but types, so the one thing it can get wrong is a `.d.ts` a
      consumer cannot read. Apollo's `FetcherRequestInit` is the type being re-shaped, so its shape is part of
      what gets checked.
    */
    "skipLibCheck": false,
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "moduleDetection": "force",
    "noEmit": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "noUncheckedSideEffectImports": true,

    /* tsc -b 的增量状态文件。 */
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.app.tsbuildinfo"
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts"]
}
